==Cast and characters==
{{See also|List of Legends of Tomorrow characters|List of Arrowverse cast members}}

* [[Caity Lotz]] as [[Sara Lance|Sara Lance / White Canary]]:<br />A [[Star City (Arrowverse)|Star City]] vigilante and former [[League of Assassins]] member suffering from rage issues after being resurrected by the mystical Lazarus Pit.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="DeadlineAnnouncement" /><ref name="White Canary" /> In the second season, Sara becomes the leader of the Legends and captain of the ''Waverider''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schwerdtfeger |first=Conner |date=March 15, 2017 |title=How Legends Of Tomorrow's Sara Lance Just Got A Lot More Important |url=https://www.cinemablend.com/television/1635640/how-legends-of-tomorrows-sara-lance-just-got-a-lot-more-important |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190729121207/https://www.cinemablend.com/television/1635640/how-legends-of-tomorrows-sara-lance-just-got-a-lot-more-important |archive-date=July 29, 2019 |access-date=July 29, 2019 |website=Cinemablend}}</ref> The character is partially based on the [[Black Canary]] and was introduced on ''Arrow''.
* [[Brandon Routh]] as [[Ray Palmer (Arrowverse)|Ray Palmer / Atom]] (seasons 1–5; guest: season 7): <br />A scientist, inventor, businessman and former CEO of Palmer Technologies who developed a power-suit that is now capable of size manipulation.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="DeadlineAnnouncement" /> In the fifth season, Ray chooses to leave the Legends to have a normal life with Nora after marrying her.<ref>{{Cite web |date=August 23, 2019 |title='DC's Legends Of Tomorrow': Brandon Routh & Courtney Ford To Depart CW Drama As Series Regulars In Season 5 |url=https://deadline.com/2019/08/brandon-routh-courtney-ford-exit-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-series-regulars-season-5-the-cw-1202702311/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190823033935/https://deadline.com/2019/08/brandon-routh-courtney-ford-exit-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-series-regulars-season-5-the-cw-1202702311/ |archive-date=August 23, 2019 |access-date=December 11, 2020 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> The character was introduced on ''[[Arrow (TV series)|Arrow]]''.
* [[Arthur Darvill]] as [[Rip Hunter (Arrowverse)|Rip Hunter]] (seasons 1–2; recurring: season 3; guest: season 7): <br />A roguish time traveler and leader of the team, who hides the strains of being responsible for history itself behind a façade of charm and wit.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="RipHunter" /> His goal is to defeat [[Vandal Savage (Arrowverse)|Vandal Savage]], his archenemy throughout time, in order to save the world and his family. Aiden Longworth portrays a young Rip Hunter.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Perry |first=Spencer |date=April 13, 2016 |title=The Team Meets Their Younger Selves in Legends of Tomorrow Episode 12 Photos |url=https://www.comingsoon.net/tv/news/676247-the-team-meets-their-younger-selves-in-legends-of-tomorrow-episode-12-photos#/slide/1 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160419052212/http://www.comingsoon.net/tv/news/676247-the-team-meets-their-younger-selves-in-legends-of-tomorrow-episode-12-photos |archive-date=April 19, 2016 |access-date=April 19, 2016 |publisher=ComingSoon.net}}</ref> In the second season, Rip disappears and gives command of the ''Waverider'' to the Legends. He later returns, first as a film student in the 1960s who has no recollection of his past life, then as a brainwashed killer working for the Legion and later back to his original self. He remains with the team for a while but departs when he realizes that the Legends no longer need him as their captain. In the third season, he is the founder and leader of the Time Bureau. At the end of season three, Rip sacrifices himself in order for the Legends to escape from the time demon, Mallus.
* [[Victor Garber]] as [[Martin Stein (Arrowverse)|Martin Stein / Firestorm]] (seasons 1–3; guest: season 7): <br />A nuclear physicist focused on transmutation and also half of the superhero Firestorm with Jefferson Jackson. During "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]", he sacrifices himself to help the heroes escape Earth-X.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="DeadlineAnnouncement" /><ref name="JacksonFirestorm" /> Graeme McComb portrays a young Stein in the 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ching |first=Albert |date=January 8, 2016 |title=Plot Synopsis for "DC's Legends of Tomorrow" Pilot Part 2 Promises Stein vs. Stein |url=https://www.cbr.com/plot-synopsis-for-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-2-promises-stein-vs-stein/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210421202244/https://www.cbr.com/plot-synopsis-for-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-2-promises-stein-vs-stein/ |archive-date=April 21, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> The character was introduced on ''[[The Flash (2014 TV series)|The Flash]]''.
* [[Franz Drameh]] as [[Jefferson Jackson (Arrowverse)|Jefferson "Jax" Jackson / Firestorm]] (seasons 1–3; guest: season 7): <br />A former [[Central City (Arrowverse)|Central City]] high school athlete whose pro career was derailed by an injury and now works as an auto mechanic.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="Drameh" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=(#204) "The Fury of Firestorm" |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/listings/20151007cw03/ |access-date=October 8, 2015 |publisher=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref> He serves as the other half of the superhero Firestorm with Martin Stein. After Stein dies, Jax decides to leave the Waverider and return to the present as he is no longer a [[metahuman]].<ref name="JacksonFirestorm">{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=September 13, 2015 |title=Legends of Tomorrow's Phil Klemmer on Fighting Nazis, Killing Characters and The Time Masters' Secret Agenda |url=https://comicbook.com/news/legends-of-tomorrows-phil-klemmer-on-fighting-nazis-killing-char/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150914051949/http://comicbook.com/2015/09/13/legends-of-tomorrows-phil-klemmer-on-fighting-nazis-killing-char/ |archive-date=September 14, 2015 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> The producers decided to create Jax as the other half of Firestorm to have him be someone in his early 20s and different from [[Ronnie Raymond (Arrowverse)|Ronnie Raymond]]'s Firestorm, bringing comedy and camaraderie with Stein.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mahadeo |first=Kevin |date=October 27, 2015 |title=Kreisberg & Panabaker on Latest "Flash" Developments and West Family Revelations |url=https://www.cbr.com/kreisberg-panabaker-on-latest-flash-developments-and-west-family-revelations/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210125031852/https://www.cbr.com/kreisberg-panabaker-on-latest-flash-developments-and-west-family-revelations/ |archive-date=January 25, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.
* [[Ciara Renée]] as [[Kendra Saunders (Arrowverse)|Kendra Saunders / Hawkgirl]] (season 1): <br />A young woman who is just beginning to learn that she has been repeatedly reincarnated over the centuries. When provoked, her ancient warrior persona manifests itself along with wings that grow out of her back.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="Hawkgirl" /><ref name="HawkmanDetails">{{Cite web |last=Almalvez |first=Laurence |date=August 8, 2015 |title='Legends of Tomorrow' EPs Tease Character Deaths, Hawkman Details |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legends-tomorrow-spoilers-hawkman-deaths-812517/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210613153220/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legends-tomorrow-spoilers-hawkman-deaths-812517/ |archive-date=June 13, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> She chooses to leave the team at the end of the first season.<ref name="HawksLeave">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=May 19, 2016 |title='DC's Legends Of Tomorrow': Ciara Renée To Depart |url=https://deadline.com/2016/05/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-ciara-renee-departs-hawkgirl-1201754078/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160521134142/http://deadline.com/2016/05/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-ciara-renee-departs-hawkgirl-1201754078/ |archive-date=May 21, 2016 |access-date=May 19, 2016 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> Saunders is also known by her Egyptian name Chay-Ara, and Edith Boardman in the series. [[Anna Deavere Smith]] portrays an older Kendra in 1871, known as [[Cinnamon (character)|Cinnamon]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=April 14, 2016 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow: "The Magnificent Eight" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/04/15/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-the-magnificent-eight-review |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160416212644/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/04/15/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-the-magnificent-eight-review |archive-date=April 16, 2016 |access-date=April 14, 2016 |publisher=[[IGN]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Ratcliffe |first=Amy |date=April 14, 2016 |title=The #DCTV Secrets of DC'S LEGENDS OF TOMORROW: Ep. 11 "The Magnificent Eight" |url=http://www.dccomics.com/blog/2016/04/14/the-dctv-secrets-of-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-ep-11-the-magnificent-eight |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160418151435/http://www.dccomics.com/blog/2016/04/14/the-dctv-secrets-of-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-ep-11-the-magnificent-eight |archive-date=April 18, 2016 |access-date=April 21, 2016 |publisher=DC Comics}}</ref> The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.
* [[Falk Hentschel]] as [[Carter Hall (Arrowverse)|Carter Hall / Hawkman]] (season 1; guest: season 7): <br />The latest reincarnation of the Egyptian prince Khufu who is fated to reincarnate throughout time along with his soulmate Kendra, with powers similar to hers.<ref name="HawkmanDetails" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Dyer |first=Mitch |date=July 11, 2015 |title=Comic Con 2015: Hawkman Coming to Legends of Tomorrow |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/07/12/comic-con-2015-hawkman-coming-to-legends-of-tomorrow |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150715232411/http://www.ign.com/articles/2015/07/12/comic-con-2015-hawkman-coming-to-legends-of-tomorrow |archive-date=July 15, 2015 |access-date=July 16, 2015 |publisher=IGN}}</ref><ref name="Hentschel">{{Cite web |last=Petski |first=Denise |date=August 3, 2015 |title=Falk Hentschel To Play Hawkman In 'Legends Of Tomorrow' |url=https://deadline.com/2015/08/falk-hentschel-cast-hawkman-legends-of-tomorrow-1201490766/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170517124347/http://deadline.com/2015/08/falk-hentschel-cast-hawkman-legends-of-tomorrow-1201490766/ |archive-date=May 17, 2017 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Byrne |first=Craig |date=August 22, 2015 |title=LEGENDS OF TOMORROW: PHIL KLEMMER TALKS HAWKMAN, ROMANCE, ATOM VS. ANT-MAN & MORE |url=http://dclegendstv.com/2015/08/22/legends-of-tomorrow-phil-klemmer-talks-hawkman-romance-atom-vs-ant-man-more/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150824190315/http://dclegendstv.com/2015/08/22/legends-of-tomorrow-phil-klemmer-talks-hawkman-romance-atom-vs-ant-man-more/ |archive-date=August 24, 2015 |publisher=DCLegendsTV}}</ref> A reincarnated version is recruited by Vandal Savage where he is known as Scythian Torvil before remembering his life as Carter Hall. He chooses to leave the team at the end of the first season.<ref name="HawksLeave" /> Hall is also known by the name Joe Boardman in the series. Hentschel received guest credit in his subsequent appearances in season one after the character's death in "Pilot, Part 2." The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.<ref name="HawksLeave" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=(#115) "Destiny" |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/listings/20160422cw07/ |access-date=April 23, 2016 |publisher=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref>
* [[Amy Pemberton]]{{Efn|Starting in season 3, Pemberton is credited as Amy Louise Pemberton.|name=|group=}} as [[Gideon (Legends of Tomorrow)|Gideon]]:<br />The artificial intelligence of the ''Waverider''.<ref name="Pemberton" /> Pemberton portrays a physical version of the character in the second-season episode, "Land of the Lost",<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=March 7, 2017 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow: "Land of the Lost" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2017/03/08/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-land-of-the-lost-review |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170308073446/http://www.ign.com/articles/2017/03/08/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-land-of-the-lost-review |archive-date=March 8, 2017 |access-date=March 8, 2017 |publisher=[[IGN]]}}</ref> the third-season episode "Here I Go Again", the fourth season episode "Legends of To-Meow-Meow", the fifth-season episode "I Am Legends", and in a regular capacity in season seven.<ref name="autogenerated1">{{Cite web |date=July 25, 2021 |title='Legends Of Tomorrow': Matt Ryan To Switch Characters, Amy Louise Pemberton To Play Human Gideon Full-Time In Season 7&nbsp;– Comic-Con |url=https://deadline.com/2021/07/legends-of-tomorrow-matt-ryan-constantine-gwyn-davies-amy-louise-pemberton-gideon-season-7-comic-con-1234799209/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210726012013/https://deadline.com/2021/07/legends-of-tomorrow-matt-ryan-constantine-gwyn-davies-amy-louise-pemberton-gideon-season-7-comic-con-1234799209/ |archive-date=July 26, 2021 |access-date=July 25, 2021}}</ref> An alternate version of Gideon (voiced by [[Morena Baccarin]]) was introduced in ''The Flash''.<ref name="Pemberton">{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=January 21, 2016 |title=Legends of Tomorrow EP Spills a Secret Behind the Big Lie&nbsp;— Plus: Grade It! |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/legends-of-tomorrow-premiere-recap-poll-676549/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160126120932/http://tvline.com/2016/01/21/legends-of-tomorrow-premiere-recap-poll/ |archive-date=January 26, 2016 |access-date=January 21, 2016 |publisher=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>
* [[Dominic Purcell]] as [[Mick Rory (Arrowverse)|Mick Rory / Heat Wave]] (seasons 1–6): <br />An arsonist, career criminal, and accomplice of Leonard Snart who, in contrast to his partner, uses a heat gun capable of burning almost anything.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="HeatWave" /> After being deserted in the past by Snart, he is recruited by the Time Masters and becomes the bounty hunter [[Chronos (character)|Chronos]], who hunts the Legends, but later rejoins the team. Mitchell Kummen portrays a young Rory.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sage |first=Alyssa |date=March 29, 2016 |title=TV News Roundup: 'Legends of Tomorrow' Casts Young Heat Wave, Shark Week Sets Premiere Date |url=https://variety.com/2016/tv/news/shark-week-2016-premiere-date-legends-of-tomorrow-young-heat-wave-mitchell-kummen-1201741391/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160330121025/http://variety.com/2016/tv/news/shark-week-2016-premiere-date-legends-of-tomorrow-young-heat-wave-mitchell-kummen-1201741391/ |archive-date=March 30, 2016 |access-date=March 30, 2016 |website=Variety}}</ref> The character was introduced on ''The Flash''. Purcell exited the series as a regular cast member after the sixth season.<ref>[https://www.instagram.com/p/CNyF5DuhAp_/]{{dead link|date=February 2022}}</ref>
* [[Wentworth Miller]] as [[Leonard Snart (Arrowverse)|Leonard Snart / Captain Cold]] (season 1; recurring: season 2; guest: season 7) and Leo Snart / Citizen Cold (recurring: season 3): <br />The son of a career criminal who turns to the quick and easy life of crime, and uses a cryonic gun to freeze objects and people on contact.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /><ref name="DeadlineAnnouncement" /> Trestyn Zradicka portrays a young Leo. At the end of the first season, Snart sacrifices himself to save his team. In the second season, the [[Legion of Doom]]<ref name="LegionOfDoom" /> recruits a past version of Snart from before he joined the team with the promise of averting his future death. Following the Legion's defeat, Mick returns Snart to the exact moment where he was recruited by the Legion, wiping his memories in the process and ensuring that Snart will eventually join the Legends. During the "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]" event, a parallel universe version from Earth-X, Leonard "Leo" Snart is introduced; Leo temporarily joins the Legends. The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.
* [[Matt Letscher]] as [[Eobard Thawne (Arrowverse)|Eobard Thawne / Reverse-Flash]] (season 2; guest: season 7): <br />A supervillain [[Speedster (fiction)|speedster]] from the future and the archenemy of the [[Barry Allen (Arrowverse)|Flash]]. He is the leader of the Legion of Doom. His goal was to keep himself from being killed by Eddie Thawne back on ''The Flash.'' In the season two finale, he is defeated by the Legends and the [[Black Flash]], apparently erasing Thawne from existence once again. The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Patton |first=Dominick |date=July 23, 2016 |title=Letscher Joins Cast; Obsidian, Stargirl & Dr. Mid-Nite Coming In Season 2&nbsp;– Comic-Con |url=https://deadline.com/2016/07/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-matt-letscher-reverse-flash-obsidian-stargirl-dr-mid-nite-1201791459/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160725141846/http://deadline.com/2016/07/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-matt-letscher-reverse-flash-obsidian-stargirl-dr-mid-nite-1201791459/ |archive-date=July 25, 2016 |access-date=July 23, 2016 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>
* [[Maisie Richardson-Sellers]] as [[Amaya Jiwe (Arrowverse)|Amaya Jiwe / Vixen]] (seasons 2–3) and [[Charlie (Arrowverse)|Charlie / Clotho]] (seasons 4–5<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gelman |first=Vlada |date=June 3, 2020 |title=Legends of Tomorrow: [Spoiler] Not Returning for Season 6 |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legends-of-tomorrow-maisie-richardson-sellers-leaving-season-6-charlie-2887494/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603081541/https://tvline.com/2020/06/02/legends-of-tomorrow-maisie-richardson-sellers-leaving-season-6-charlie/ |archive-date=June 3, 2020 |access-date=June 3, 2020}}</ref>): <br />A member of the [[Justice Society of America]] in the 1940s who is able to magically channel the abilities of the animal kingdom thanks to the mysterious Tantu Totem. She is the grandmother of [[Mari McCabe (Arrowverse)|Mari McCabe]], who is portrayed by [[Megalyn Echikunwoke]] in other Arrowverse series.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Siegel |first=Lucas |date=June 23, 2016 |title=Maisie Richardson-Sellers is DC's Legends of Tomorrow's New Vixen |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/maisie-richardson-sellers-is-dcs-legends-of-tomorrows-new-vixen/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210225044426/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/maisie-richardson-sellers-is-dcs-legends-of-tomorrows-new-vixen/ |archive-date=February 25, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |publisher=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> It was originally intended for the McCabe version of Vixen to be used in ''Legends'' as well, but Echikunwoke was unable to reprise the role due to previous commitments.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Holbrook |first=Damian |date=June 7, 2016 |title=''DC's Legends of Tomorrow'' Recruits Vixen... With a Twist! |url=https://www.tvinsider.com/90519/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-recruits-vixen-with-a-twist/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160609082958/http://www.tvinsider.com/article/90519/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-recruits-vixen-with-a-twist/ |archive-date=June 9, 2016 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=TV Insider}}</ref> At the end of season 3, she returns to Zambesi. Charlie is introduced in season 4 as a "magical fugitive who slips through" the rift the Waverider crew opened. She is a shapeshifter who takes the form of Amaya  during a fight with the Legends in the hopes that they will not attack a friend. She is frozen into that shape during the encounter and captured by the Legends. She eventually gets her magical powers back, but continues to use Amaya's form. She is a formidable fighter and knows a great deal about the other magical fugitives.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gelman |first=Vlada |date=July 21, 2018 |title='Legends' @ Comic-Con: [Spoiler]'s New Character Revealed, 'Avalance' Update and... a Beatles Cameo? |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-spoilers-comic-con-panel-963713/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180722063516/https://tvline.com/2018/07/21/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-spoilers-comic-con-panel/ |archive-date=July 22, 2018 |access-date=July 22, 2018 |website=TVLine}}</ref>
* [[Nick Zano]] as [[Nate Heywood (Arrowverse)|Nate Heywood / Steel]] (seasons 2–7):<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=March 2, 2022 |title='Legends of Tomorrow' star explains their decision to leave and 'honorable exit' |url=https://ew.com/tv/legends-of-tomorrow-nick-zano-exit-season-7-finale/ |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220303020949/https://ew.com/tv/legends-of-tomorrow-nick-zano-exit-season-7-finale/ |archive-date=March 3, 2022 |access-date=March 3, 2022}}</ref> <br />A historian from Star City who gains the ability to transform himself into a steel-like form, and is the grandson of [[Commander Steel#Henry Heywood|Commander Steel]], a member of the Justice Society of America.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Andreeva |first1=Nellie |last2=Lincoln |first2=Ross |date=June 15, 2016 |title='DC's Legends Of Tomorrow': Nick Zano Joins As New Hero With Steel Pedigree |url=https://deadline.com/2016/06/nick-zano-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-2-steel-nate-heywood-1201773397/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160616074940/http://deadline.com/2016/06/nick-zano-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-2-steel-nate-heywood-1201773397/ |archive-date=June 16, 2016 |access-date=June 15, 2016 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_E-XwxO0uc |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow {{!}} Nick Zano Interview |date=October 6, 2016 |last=The CW Network |publisher=[[YouTube]] |time=0:10 |access-date=October 6, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170622055114/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r_E-XwxO0uc |archive-date=June 22, 2017 |url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[Tala Ashe]] as [[Zari Tomaz]] (seasons 3–4; recurring: seasons 5–7) and Zari Tarazi (seasons 5–7): <br />A computer hacker from the year 2042 who possesses aerokinetic powers from a mystical amulet.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Stanhope |first=Kate |date=June 6, 2017 |title='Legends of Tomorrow' Season 3 Adds Muslim-American Superhero |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legends-tomorrow-season-3-muslim-american-superhero-1010692/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322182437/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/legends-tomorrow-season-3-muslim-american-superhero-1010692/ |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> At the end of season four, the future where Zari came from changes, resulting in her disappearing and being replaced by her brother [[Behrad Tarazi]] with the Legends having no memory of her. In the new future, Zari is a socialite named Zari Tarazi, who eventually joins the Legends, wielding the air totem along with her brother, Behrad. The original Zari lives within the totem.
* [[Keiynan Lonsdale]] as [[Wally West (Arrowverse)|Wally West / Kid Flash]] (season 3): <br />A speedster from [[Keystone City]], and later Central City, who was mentored by [[Barry Allen (Arrowverse)|Barry Allen]]. He is the son of [[Joe West (Arrowverse)|Joe West]] and the brother of [[Iris West (Arrowverse)|Iris West]], and looking for his place in the world. The character was introduced on ''The Flash''.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last1=Agard |first1=Chancellor |last2=Abrams |first2=Natalie |date=January 19, 2018 |title=Legends of Tomorrow adds Keiynan Lonsdale as series regular |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/01/19/legends-of-tomorrow-adds-keiynan-lonsdale-as-series-regular/ |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180119235248/http://ew.com/tv/2018/01/19/legends-of-tomorrow-adds-keiynan-lonsdale-as-series-regular/ |archive-date=January 19, 2018 |access-date=January 19, 2018}}</ref><ref name="LonsdaleExit">{{Cite web |last=Webb Mitovich |first=Matt |date=June 5, 2018 |title=''Legends'' Season 4: Keiynan Lonsdale Not Returning as Series Regular |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-keiynan-lonsdale-leaving-series-regular-953061/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180814102622/https://tvline.com/2018/06/05/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-keiynan-lonsdale-leaving-series-regular/ |archive-date=August 14, 2018 |access-date=August 4, 2018 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>
* [[Jes Macallan]] as [[Ava Sharpe]] (seasons 4–7; recurring: season 3): <br />The former Director of the Time Bureau and girlfriend of Sara Lance. In season three it is revealed that she is a clone from the year 2213. In season five, after the Time Bureau is shut down, she became a permanent member of the Legends, eventually becoming co-captain alongside Sara.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=April 3, 2018 |title=''Legends of Tomorrow'' promotes Jes Macallan to series regular for season 4 |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/04/03/legends-of-tomorrow-jes-macallan-series-regular-season-4/ |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180404041657/http://ew.com/tv/2018/04/03/legends-of-tomorrow-jes-macallan-series-regular-season-4/ |archive-date=April 4, 2018 |access-date=April 3, 2018}}</ref> In season 6, she marries Sara.<ref>{{Cite web |date=June 21, 2021 |title=Legends Of Tomorrow serves up a dumpster full of love fireworks |url=https://www.avclub.com/legends-of-tomorrow-serves-up-a-dumpster-full-of-love-f-1847139491 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210629162942/https://www.avclub.com/legends-of-tomorrow-serves-up-a-dumpster-full-of-love-f-1847139491 |archive-date=June 29, 2021 |access-date=June 29, 2021 |website=The A.V. Club}}</ref>
* [[Matt Ryan (actor)|Matt Ryan]] as [[John Constantine (Arrowverse)|John Constantine]] (seasons 4–6; recurring: season 3) and [[List of Legends of Tomorrow characters#Gwyn Davies|Gwyn Davies]] (season 7): <br />An English magician/warlock, occult detective, and [[Confidence trick|con man]]. Ryan is listed among the main cast but receives a special appearance credit. Ryan was announced as being promoted to a series regular for the fourth season ahead of its renewal, reprising his role as Constantine from the short-lived series ''[[Constantine (TV series)|Constantine]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=March 19, 2018 |title=Matt Ryan To Join 'DC's Legends Of Tomorrow' As Series Regular For Season 4 |url=https://deadline.com/2018/03/matt-ryan-promoted-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-series-regular-season-4-renewal-john-constantine-1202345972/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190412184919/https://deadline.com/2018/03/matt-ryan-promoted-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-series-regular-season-4-renewal-john-constantine-1202345972/ |archive-date=April 12, 2019 |access-date=March 20, 2018 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> In season seven, Ryan portrayed a new character named Dr. Gwyn Davies, an eccentric scientist from the early 20th century.<ref name="autogenerated1" />
* [[Courtney Ford]] as [[Nora Darhk]] (seasons 4–5; recurring: season 3; guest: season 7): <br />The daughter of the deceased super-villain [[Damien Darhk (Arrowverse)|Damien Darhk]] and the love interest (later wife) of Ray Palmer. The character's younger self was introduced on ''Arrow''.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Andreeva |first1=Nellie |last2=Petski |first2=Denise |date=June 22, 2018 |title='Legends Of Tomorrow': Courtney Ford Upped To Series Regular For Season 4 |url=https://deadline.com/2018/06/legends-of-tomorrow-courtney-ford-promoted-series-regular-nora-dahrk-the-cw-1202415971/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181122092151/https://deadline.com/2018/06/legends-of-tomorrow-courtney-ford-promoted.-series-regular-nora-dahrk-the-cw-1202415971/ |archive-date=November 22, 2018 |access-date=November 22, 2018 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref>
* [[Ramona Young]] as [[Mona Wu]] (season 4; recurring: season 5): <br />A young woman obsessed with fantasy novels who is "something of an expert in the world of the magical creatures that the Legends encounter". She works for the Time Bureau.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nemetz |first=Dave |date=July 21, 2018 |title=DC's Legends Adds Supernatural Whiz, Back to the Future's Biff for Season 4 |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-cast-ramona-young-tom-wilson-966095/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180722020436/https://tvline.com/2018/07/21/legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-cast-ramona-young-tom-wilson/ |archive-date=July 22, 2018 |access-date=July 22, 2018 |website=TVLine}}</ref> She leaves the Waverider in season 5 to assume the Rebecca Silver pen name from Mick Rory.<ref>{{Cite web |date=January 21, 2020 |title=Allow the Legends Of Tomorrow to re-introduce themselves in a raucous post-Crisis premiere |url=https://www.avclub.com/allow-the-legends-of-tomorrow-to-re-introduce-themselve-1841146784 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210629162940/https://www.avclub.com/allow-the-legends-of-tomorrow-to-re-introduce-themselve-1841146784 |archive-date=June 29, 2021 |access-date=June 29, 2021 |website=The A.V. Club}}</ref>
* [[Olivia Swann]] as [[Astra Logue (Arrowverse)|Astra Logue]] (seasons 5–7; guest: season 4)<br />A woman damned to hell as a child following a botched exorcism by Constantine. Now an adult, she had become determined to rise to the top of hell's food chain.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=July 11, 2019 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow ups Astra actress to series regular for season 5 |url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/07/11/legends-of-tomorrow-olivia-swann-astra-season-5-big-bad/ |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190714040134/https://ew.com/tv/2019/05/16/arrowverse-crisis-on-infinite-earths-details/ |archive-date=July 14, 2019 |access-date=July 12, 2019}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Damore |first=Meagan |date=July 11, 2019 |title=Legends of Tomorrow S5's Villain Is a Constantine Mainstay |work=[[Comic Book Resources]] |url=https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-season-5-villain-astra/ |url-status=live |access-date=July 12, 2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190711223732/https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-season-5-villain-astra/ |archive-date=July 11, 2019}}</ref> However, after helping the Legends defeat the Fates, Astra moves in to Constantine's house, and wants to try living a normal life on Earth.
* [[Adam Tsekhman]] as [[Gary Green (Arrowverse)|Gary Green]] (seasons 6–7; recurring: seasons 3–5): <br />A Time Bureau Agent serving under Director Rip Hunter when it was founded with the goal of protecting and preserving the timeline. After Hunter is arrested and removed from office when he violates Time Bureau Code, Gary serves under Agent and later Director Ava Sharpe as her most loyal and often very obsessed Time Bureau Agent. After being easily manipulated by Director Sharpe, John Constantine, and the Legends, along with being mistreated by them, Gary betrays the team and joins Neron and Tabitha in their quest to bring the demons and the denizens of Hell over on Earth. However, after seeing that Neron and Tabitha do not care about him, Gary regrets his decision and rejoins the Legends; aiding them in destroying Neron and Tabitha for good. For his actions, Gary is made a part-time member of the Legends, and becomes John Constantine's sorcerer apprentice. Gary and Constantine continue to aid the Legends, joining up with them to rescue Astra Logue from Hell, and to stop the Encores and the evil Fates Lachesis and Atropos from enslaving humanity. When Charlie leaves the Legends after the defeat of Lachesis and Atropos, Gary is made a full time member of the Legends and rejoins them along with Constantine.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Childs |first=Kelvin |date=October 1, 2020 |title=Legends of Tomorrow: Gary Green Officially Joins the Team in Season 6 |url=https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-gary-green-joins-season-6/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201008131633/https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-gary-green-joins-season-6/ |archive-date=October 8, 2020 |access-date=October 1, 2020 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref> In season six, Gary is revealed to be an alien of the Necrian species who uses his glasses to disguise himself as a human.
* [[Shayan Sobhian]] as [[Behrad Tarazi]] (seasons 6–7; recurring: season 5; guest: season 4): <br />Zari Tomaz's deceased brother, who, during the season four finale, is resurrected, replacing Zari in the team after she alters the timeline. In season five, he is killed by [[Atropos]], but resurrected once more, and is now a permanent wielder of the air totem along with his sister, Zari Tarazi, the version of Zari created when history was changed.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gelman |first=Vlada |date=June 17, 2020 |title=Legends Promotes Shayan Sobhian to Series Regular for Season 6 |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legends-of-tomorrow-season-6-shayan-sobhian-series-regular-behrad-2887936/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200617185140/https://tvline.com/2020/06/17/legends-of-tomorrow-season-6-shayan-sobhian-series-regular-behrad/ |archive-date=June 17, 2020 |access-date=June 17, 2020 |website=TVLine}}</ref>
* [[Lisseth Chavez]] as [[Esperanza "Spooner" Cruz]] (seasons 6–7): <br />Esperanza is a "tough and self-sufficient" woman who "lives off the grid, devising ingenious tech for the detection of&nbsp;– and defense against&nbsp;– space aliens [...] and while some might call her paranoid, she calls it being prepared. A survivor of a childhood alien encounter, Spooner now believes she has the ability to communicate telepathically with aliens".<ref name="Spooner">{{Cite web |last=Gelman |first=Vlada |date=September 12, 2020 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Adds Chicago P.D. Vet Lisseth Chavez as Series Regular |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/legends-of-tomorrow-season-6-lisseth-chavez-cast-series-regular-spooner-1234574831/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200916005618/https://tvline.com/2020/09/12/legends-of-tomorrow-season-6-lisseth-chavez-cast-series-regular-spooner/ |archive-date=September 16, 2020 |access-date=September 12, 2020 |website=TVLine}}</ref>

[[LaMonica Garrett]] is credited as a main character in "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths: Part Five]]" for playing the [[Anti-Monitor (Arrowverse)|Anti-Monitor]], an evil being dedicated to ending the [[Multiverse (DC Comics)|multiverse]], and the polar opposite of [[Monitor (Arrowverse)|Mar Novu / Monitor]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Damore |first=Meagan |date=November 16, 2019 |title=Crisis on Infinite Earths' LaMonica Garrett Introduces the Anti-Monitor |url=https://www.cbr.com/crisis-infinite-earths-lamonica-garrett-anti-monitor-interview/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20191117051907/https://www.cbr.com/crisis-infinite-earths-lamonica-garrett-anti-monitor-interview/ |archive-date=November 17, 2019 |access-date=November 20, 2019 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref>

==Production==
===Development===
In January 2015, co-creator [[Greg Berlanti]] stated that there were "very early" preliminary talks for an additional spin-off series centered on [[Ray Palmer (Arrowverse)|Ray Palmer/Atom]] ([[Brandon Routh]]), from ''[[Arrow (TV series)|Arrow]]'' and ''[[The Flash (2014 TV series)|The Flash]]''.<ref name="AtomSpinoff" /> In February 2015, it was reported that a spin-off series, described as a superhero team-up show, was in discussion by The CW for a possible [[2015–16 United States network television schedule|2015–16]] midseason release. Berlanti, [[Andrew Kreisberg]], [[Marc Guggenheim]], and Sarah Schechter would serve as executive producers. The potential series would be headlined by several recurring characters from both ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash'', including Palmer, [[Leonard Snart (Arrowverse)|Leonard Snart]] ([[Wentworth Miller]]), and [[Martin Stein (Arrowverse)|Dr. Martin Stein]] ([[Victor Garber]]). [[Caity Lotz]] was also mentioned to be among the main cast. There would be potential for other ''Arrow''/''Flash'' characters to cross over to the new series, and the series would be casting "three major DC Comics characters who have never appeared in a TV series".<ref name="DeadlineAnnouncement" />

In March 2015, [[Stephen Amell]], who portrays [[Oliver Queen (Arrowverse)|Oliver Queen/Green Arrow]] on ''Arrow'', confirmed the series would air in the 2015–16 midseason. Additionally, Kreisberg stated more would be revealed about the nature of the series by the end of ''Arrow''{{'}}s third season, specifically why Lotz is slated to appear, given her previous character, Sara, was killed at the start of ''Arrow'' season three.<ref name="ScreenRantMarch2015" /> Berlanti also stated there was a particular reason for the other half of Firestorm—[[Ronnie Raymond (Arrowverse)|Ronnie Raymond]] ([[Robbie Amell]]), as seen on ''The Flash''—not being mentioned in the initial cast announcement.<ref name="RonnieRaymond" /> On the purpose of the series, Berlanti said it was designed to be "most similar to our crossover episodes, where you feel that 'event-iness', but all the time. For us, first and foremost, with all of [our shows], it's about 'how is it its own thing?' Because we don't just want to do it to do it." He also revealed the producers were focusing on "making sure that the villain that we have on [the] show is distinct too... another big character who hasn't been used yet."<ref name="VarietyMarch2015" /> Also in March, [[Dominic Purcell]] was revealed to be reprising his role as [[Mick Rory (Arrowverse)|Heat Wave]] in the series (noteworthy, reuniting Purcell with his ''[[Prison Break]]'' Co-Star Wentworth Miller),<ref name="HeatWave" /> and [[Blake Neely]], composer of ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash'', would serve as composer.<ref name="NeelyConfirm" /> At the end of the month, [[Arthur Darvill]] was cast as [[Rip Hunter (Arrowverse)|Rip Hunter]], one of the "new to TV" DC characters,<ref name="RipHunter" /> while [[Ciara Renée]] was cast as [[Kendra Saunders (Arrowverse)|Kendra Saunders / Hawkgirl]].<ref name="Hawkgirl" /> In April 2015, in a ''[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]'' article on the recent [[MIPTV Media Market|MipTV]] event, it noted the title for the series would be ''Legends of Tomorrow'', despite it still being unconfirmed by those involved with the series.<ref name="VarietyTitleApr2015" /> Also in the month, [[Franz Drameh]] was cast as [[Jefferson Jackson (Arrowverse)|Jax Jackson]].<ref name="Drameh" />

In May 2015, actor Victor Garber said that The CW was impressed with what was shown to them, giving the project a straight-to-series order.<ref name="January2016">{{Cite web |last=Dyce |first=Andrew |date=May 2, 2015 |title='The Flash/Arrow' Spinoff Going Straight to Series; Premieres January 2016 |url=https://screenrant.com/flash-arrow-spinoff-show-premiere-date-2016/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150503204344/http://screenrant.com/flash-arrow-spinoff-show-premiere-date-2016/ |archive-date=May 3, 2015 |access-date=May 2, 2015 |publisher=Screen Rant}}</ref> The network officially confirmed the order for the series on May 7, 2015, as well as the official title, ''DC's Legends of Tomorrow''.<ref name="SeriesOrdered" /> Later in the month, it was confirmed that Lotz would reprise her role as [[Sara Lance]], who would be taking the name [[White Canary]],<ref name="White Canary" /> as well as revealing the antagonist as [[Vandal Savage (Arrowverse)|Vandal Savage]].<ref name="VandalSavage" /> In June 2015, it was announced that [[Phil Klemmer]] had been made the series [[showrunner]] as well as executive producer;<ref name="Klemmer" /> Chris Fedak serves as executive producer and co-showrunner with Klemmer.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=September 14, 2016 |title=ABC Buys FBI Drama From Chris Fedak, Magician David Kwong & Berlanti TV |url=https://deadline.com/2016/09/deception-fbi-drama-chris-fedak-david-kwong-greg-berlati-1201819327/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160915085855/http://deadline.com/2016/09/deception-fbi-drama-chris-fedak-david-kwong-greg-berlati-1201819327/ |archive-date=September 15, 2016 |access-date=September 14, 2016 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> In July 2015, Klemmer and Guggenheim likened ''Legends of Tomorrow'' to an [[anthology series]] as "not everybody will be continuing on this journey", with each season being "its own separate movie" but not disconnected from each other in the manner of ''[[True Detective]]'' or ''[[American Horror Story]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 21, 2015 |title='DC's Legends of Tomorrow' Showrunner Compares Series To 'Ocean's 11' |url=https://screenrant.com/dc-legends-tomorrow-arrow-flash-comparisons/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210525092233/https://screenrant.com/dc-legends-tomorrow-arrow-flash-comparisons/ |archive-date=May 25, 2021 |access-date=May 25, 2021 |website=Screen Rant}}</ref> However, the anthology format was dropped, though the series did go through numerous changes in cast gradually.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 1, 2021 |title=The Arrowverse Almost Had The First DC TV Anthology Series |url=https://screenrant.com/arrowverse-anthology-series-legends-tomorrow-original-plan/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210525092231/https://screenrant.com/arrowverse-anthology-series-legends-tomorrow-original-plan/ |archive-date=May 25, 2021 |access-date=May 25, 2021 |website=Screen Rant}}</ref> In August 2015, [[Casper Crump]] was cast as Vandal Savage.<ref name="Crump">{{Cite web |last=Roots |first=Kimberly |date=August 4, 2015 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Casts Season 1 Big Bad Vandal Savage |url=https://tvline.com/2015/08/04/legends-of-tomorrow-vandal-savage-casper-crump-cast/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150806000812/http://tvline.com/2015/08/04/legends-of-tomorrow-vandal-savage-casper-crump-cast/ |archive-date=August 6, 2015 |access-date=August 4, 2015 |publisher=TVLine}}</ref>

On March 11, 2016, the series was renewed for a second season,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=March 11, 2016 |title='The Flash', 'The 100' and even 'Crazy Ex-Girlfriend' renewed: All 11 CW series picked up for 2016–17 |url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/03/11/the-flash-the-100-and-even-crazy-ex-girlfriend-renewed-all-11-cw-series-picked-up-for-2016-17/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160312010604/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2016/03/11/the-flash-the-100-and-even-crazy-ex-girlfriend-renewed-all-11-cw-series-picked-up-for-2016-17/ |archive-date=March 12, 2016 |access-date=March 11, 2016 |website=TV by the Numbers}}</ref> which debuted in October 2016.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ge |first=Linda |date=May 19, 2016 |title='Supergirl' Could Lose Calista Flockhart as Series Regular in Season 2 |url=https://www.thewrap.com/supergirl-could-lose-calista-flockhart-as-series-regular-in-season-2/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160521181539/http://www.thewrap.com/supergirl-could-lose-calista-flockhart-as-series-regular-in-season-2/ |archive-date=May 21, 2016 |access-date=May 19, 2016 |publisher=The Wrap}}</ref> The producers have considered adjusting the Legends team for additional seasons, with [[Joseph David-Jones]]' [[Connor Hawke (Arrowverse Earth-16)|Connor Hawke]] and [[Megalyn Echikunwoke]]'s [[Mari McCabe (Arrowverse)|Vixen]] potential additions.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gallaway |first=Lauren |date=March 2, 2016 |title=David-Jones Discusses Connor Hawke's Possible Return to "Legends of Tomorrow" |url=https://www.cbr.com/david-jones-discusses-connor-hawkes-possible-return-to-legends-of-tomorrow/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210125025810/https://www.cbr.com/david-jones-discusses-connor-hawkes-possible-return-to-legends-of-tomorrow/ |archive-date=January 25, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldman |first=Eric |date=January 10, 2016 |title=Vixen Animated Series Renewed for Season 2; CW Ponders More in Live-Action |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/10/vixen-animated-series-renewed-for-season-2-cw-ponders-more-in-live-action |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160110191531/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/10/vixen-animated-series-renewed-for-season-2-cw-ponders-more-in-live-action |archive-date=January 10, 2016 |access-date=January 10, 2016 |publisher=IGN}}</ref> For the second season, Klemmer revealed that ''Arrow'' writer [[Keto Shimizu]] and ''The Flash'' writer [[Grainne Godfree]] would be working on ''Legends'' in order to "make our stories work in concert" with ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash''. Klemmer also noted the challenges of creating more crossover elements, since Amell and Gustin work full days for their respective shows. In terms of working within the Arrowverse, Klemmer said that the death of Laurel Lance on ''Arrow'' would "resonate into Season 2... [since] something that happens on ''Arrow'' can create ripples that appear on our show in a huge way. It fundamentally alters the DNA of our series."<ref name="KlemmerIGN">{{Cite web |last=Schwartz |first=Terri |date=April 27, 2016 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow: Phil Klemmer on Arrow Crossover, Season 2 Villains |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/04/27/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-phil-klemmer-on-arrow-crossover-season-2-villains |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160429113929/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/04/27/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-phil-klemmer-on-arrow-crossover-season-2-villains |archive-date=April 29, 2016 |access-date=April 28, 2016 |publisher=[[IGN]]}}</ref> The second season initially consisted of 13 episodes,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovitch |first=Matt Webb |date=August 11, 2016 |title=CW Boss on Fifth Superhero Night, Supergirl Predictions, Episode Counts, Little Women Status and More |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-new-superhero-series-arrow-spinoff-2017-740344/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160812004007/http://tvline.com/2016/08/11/the-cw-new-superhero-series-arrow-spinoff-2017/ |archive-date=August 12, 2016 |access-date=August 11, 2016 |publisher=TVLine}}</ref> with four more ordered in November 2016 to bring the season total to 17.<ref name="S2MoreEps">{{Cite web |last=O'Connell |first=Michael |date=November 9, 2016 |title=The CW Orders More 'Legends of Tomorrow' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/cw-orders-more-legends-tomorrow-945991/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161110115451/http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/live-feed/cw-orders-more-legends-tomorrow-945991 |archive-date=November 10, 2016 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref>

Teasing the premise of season two in April 2016, Klemmer stated, "We're coming at it from a completely different angle. We're determined to make every part of season two feel like its own show. [The first episode of season two] will very much be a new pilot with new good guys, new bad guys, new stakes, new dynamics, new goals. The team will basically have to find a new purpose. Once you save the world, what do you do then?... The fact that the world was in peril sort of forced our team to fall into its own dysfunctional version of lockstep. Season two, they're no longer going to be hunted by Time Masters. They're no longer going to be burdened with having to save the world. It's no longer going to be about saving Miranda and Jonas. The interesting thing about season two is I think it's going to have a much, much different tone because our Legends are going to have a totally different purpose. They're actually going to have a totally different constitution. There will be new faces and new everything."<ref name="KlemmerIGN" /> The season also introduced members of the [[Justice Society of America]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=May 19, 2016 |title=Legends of Tomorrow to introduce Justice Society of America in season 2 |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/05/19/legends-tomorrow-justice-society-season-2 |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160523063024/http://www.ew.com/article/2016/05/19/legends-tomorrow-justice-society-season-2 |archive-date=May 23, 2016 |access-date=May 19, 2016}}</ref> The Society consisted of [[Rex Tyler (Arrowverse)|Hourman]], [[Amaya Jiwe|Vixen]], [[Henry Heywood (Arrowverse)|Commander Steel]], [[Todd Rice (Arrowverse)|Obsidian]], [[Courtney Whitmore (Arrowverse)|Stargirl]], and [[Charles McNider (Arrowverse)|Dr. Mid-Nite]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=September 30, 2016 |title=Meet the Justice Society of America in new Legends of Tomorrow photos |url=https://www.ew.com/article/2016/09/30/legends-tomorrow-justice-society-photos |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161001164638/http://www.ew.com/article/2016/09/30/legends-tomorrow-justice-society-photos |archive-date=October 1, 2016 |access-date=October 1, 2016}}</ref> The season also featured a version of the [[Legion of Doom]], composed of the [[Eobard Thawne (Arrowverse)|Reverse-Flash]], [[Malcolm Merlyn (Arrowverse)|Malcolm Merlyn]], [[Damien Darhk (Arrowverse)|Damien Darhk]], and Leonard Snart.<ref name="LegionOfDoom">{{Cite web |last=Danmore |first=Meghan |date=July 23, 2016 |title=SDCC: "DC's Legends of Tomorrow" Welcomes the Justice Society of America & More |url=https://www.cbr.com/sdcc-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-welcomes-the-justice-society-of-america-more/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210126080148/https://www.cbr.com/sdcc-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-welcomes-the-justice-society-of-america-more/ |archive-date=January 26, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref>

''Legends of Tomorrow'' was renewed for a [[Legends of Tomorrow season 4|fourth season]] which premiered on October 22, 2018.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=April 2, 2018 |title='Riverdale,' 'Flash,' 'Supernatural' Among 10 CW Renewals |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/riverdale-flash-supernatural-10-cw-renewals-1098997/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211007083322/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/riverdale-flash-supernatural-10-cw-renewals-1098997/ |archive-date=October 7, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Swift |first=Andy |date=June 20, 2018 |title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates, Including New 'Super' Sunday |language=en-US |work=TVLine |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/cw-premiere-dates-fall-2018-flash-charmed-riverdale-954928/ |url-status=live |access-date=June 20, 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180620225706/https://tvline.com/2018/06/20/cw-premiere-dates-fall-2018-flash-charmed-riverdale/ |archive-date=June 20, 2018}}</ref> On January 31, 2019, The CW renewed the series for a [[Legends of Tomorrow season 5|fifth season]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=January 31, 2019 |title=CW Renews 'The Flash,' 'Charmed,' 'Riverdale,' 'Supernatural,' 6 More |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/cw-renews-flash-charmed-riverdale-supernatural-6-more-1181714/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220315011000/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/cw-renews-flash-charmed-riverdale-supernatural-6-more-1181714/ |archive-date=March 15, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> The fifth season debuted following the midseason break in January 2020.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=May 16, 2019 |title=The CW reveals fall 2019 schedule: Batwoman and Supergirl team up on Sunday |url=https://ew.com/tv/2019/05/16/cw-fall-2019-schedule-batwoman-nancy-drew/ |url-status=live |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190517071156/https://ew.com/tv/2019/05/16/cw-fall-2019-schedule-batwoman-nancy-drew/ |archive-date=May 17, 2019 |access-date=May 16, 2019}}</ref><ref name="CrisisTwoQuarters">{{Cite web |last=Boucher |first=Geoff |date=May 16, 2019 |title='Arrowverse' Endgame? CW Chief Details 'Crisis On Infinite Earths' Mega-Event |url=https://deadline.com/2019/05/arrowverse-endgame-cw-chief-details-crisis-on-infinite-earths-mega-event-1202616631/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190516215950/https://deadline.com/2019/05/arrowverse-endgame-cw-chief-details-crisis-on-infinite-earths-mega-event-1202616631/ |archive-date=May 16, 2019 |access-date=May 16, 2019 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> On January 7, 2020, the series was renewed for a sixth season, which premiered on May 2, 2021.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ausiello |first=Michael |date=January 7, 2020 |title=CW Renews Riverdale, Batwoman, Roswell, Black Lightning Plus 9 Others |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-renewed-shows-2020-list-riverdale-flash-1142188/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200108032431/https://tvline.com/2020/01/07/the-cw-renewed-shows-2020-list-riverdale-flash/ |archive-date=January 8, 2020 |access-date=January 7, 2020 |website=TVLine}}</ref><ref name="S6Premiere">{{Cite web |last=Pedersen |first=Erik |date=February 24, 2021 |title=The CW Sets Premiere Dates For 'Kung Fu', 'Republic Of Sarah' & Return Of 'Dynasty', 'Legends Of Tomorrow', 'In The Dark'; New Slots For 'Batwoman', 'Charmed' |url=https://deadline.com/2021/02/cw-premiere-dates-kung-fu-republic-of-sarah-dynasty-legends-of-tomorrow-batwoman-charmed-1234700057/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210224200138/https://deadline.com/2021/02/cw-premiere-dates-kung-fu-republic-of-sarah-dynasty-legends-of-tomorrow-batwoman-charmed-1234700057/ |archive-date=February 24, 2021 |access-date=February 24, 2021 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> On February 3, 2021, the series was renewed for a seventh season which premiered on October 13, 2021,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=February 3, 2021 |title='Walker,' 'Flash,' 'Riverdale' Among 12 CW Shows to Score Early Renewals |url=https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/walker-renewed-season-2-cw-flash-riverdale-legends-of-tomorrow-1234899745/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210210211922/https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/walker-renewed-season-2-cw-flash-riverdale-legends-of-tomorrow-1234899745/ |archive-date=February 10, 2021 |access-date=February 4, 2021 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=June 15, 2021 |title=The CW Sets Fall Premiere Dates for ''The Flash'', ''Walker'', ''4400'' and 11 Others |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-the-flash-walker-riverdale-1234683482/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210616040119/https://tvline.com/2021/06/15/the-cw-fall-premiere-dates-the-flash-walker-riverdale/ |archive-date=June 16, 2021 |access-date=June 15, 2021 |website=TVLine}}</ref> and the series finale aired on March 2, 2022.<ref name="TFCMarch022022">{{Cite web |title=LISTINGS, wednesday, march 02, 2022 |url=http://www.thefutoncritic.com/listings/2022/03/02/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20220731043948/http://www.thefutoncritic.com/listings/2022/03/02/ |archive-date=July 31, 2022 |access-date=January 22, 2022 |website=[[The Futon Critic]]}}</ref>

===Filming===
In May 2015, Garber revealed filming would begin in August 2015, for a January 2016 premiere.<ref name="January2016" /> The series shot a presentation for the network's [[upfronts|upfront showcase]], which was filmed over the course of one night, and directed by ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash'' veteran [[Dermott Downs]].<ref name="JacksonFirestorm" /> Filming of the series began on September 9, 2015, in [[Vancouver, British Columbia]].<ref>{{Cite tweet |number=641634706404933633 |user=mguggenheim |title=Legends of Tomorrow begins production today. @GBerlanti @AJKreisberg @philklemmer @Glen__Winter |date=September 9, 2015 |access-date=September 9, 2015 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151104142953/https://twitter.com/mguggenheim/status/641634706404933633 |archive-date=November 4, 2015 |url-status=live |first=Marc |last=Guggenheim}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Lotz |first=Caity |date=September 5, 2015 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow table read! Stuff is about to go down when filming begins on Wednesday! #LegendsInTheMaking |url=https://www.facebook.com/caitylotz/posts/1127054470642675 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20151129134601/https://www.facebook.com/caitylotz/posts/1127054470642675%23 |archive-date=November 29, 2015 |access-date=September 5, 2015 |publisher=Facebook}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hayner |first=Chris |date=January 20, 2016 |title=6 'Legends of Tomorrow' teases that prove it's nothing like 'Arrow' or 'The Flash' |url=http://zap2it.com/2016/01/legends-of-tomorrow-premiere-teases-arrow-the-flash/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160128083225/http://zap2it.com/2016/01/legends-of-tomorrow-premiere-teases-arrow-the-flash/ |archive-date=January 28, 2016 |access-date=January 29, 2016 |publisher=Zap2it}}</ref> Director/producer [[Glen Winter]] discussed in a January 2016 interview with ''[[Comic Book Resources]]'' the process of filming key elements of the series' pilot,
<blockquote>The new facet for ''Legends'' was that there's no #1 [actor] on the call sheet. There are seven or eight leads. For me, that was the intimidating part. I wasn't as worried about the action and tone as I was with wrangling all these personalities and finding out how they all work together. Or, how to shoot a scene with eight people in the Waverider, day after day.<ref name="Winter">{{Cite web |last=Cairns |first=Brian |date=January 29, 2016 |title="Legends of Tomorrow" Director Promises To "Push the Boundaries" of Superhero Action |url=https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-director-promises-to-push-the-boundaries-of-superhero-action/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210125032555/https://www.cbr.com/legends-of-tomorrow-director-promises-to-push-the-boundaries-of-superhero-action/ |archive-date=January 25, 2021 |access-date=January 29, 2016 |website=[[Comic Book Resources]]}}</ref></blockquote> He stated of the series style of shooting on location as opposed to predominantly shooting on a [[soundstage]],
<blockquote>As is typical with any pilot, most of the time you are going to shoot more on location. Because you don't necessarily know if you are going to have a show that's been picked up, they don't want to invest a lot of money in the infrastructure, so you end up shooting more on location. The only set that was built was the Waverider. That being said, because we knew there was a pickup for the show, it wasn't a conventional pilot. All the resources of construction went into the Waverider. That's continuing into the series. I don't think they tend to build much. I think they tend to adapt locations because there's so much time travel and so many eras to create.<ref name="Winter" /></blockquote>

===Music===
''[[Arrow (TV series)|Arrow]]'', ''[[The Flash (2014 TV series)|The Flash]]'', and ''[[Supergirl (TV series)|Supergirl]]'' composer [[Blake Neely]] was also hired for this series. All soundtracks and singles are released by [[WaterTower Music]]. The first season soundtrack was released on August 31, 2016,<ref>{{Cite web |title=DC's Legends Of Tomorrow: Original Television Soundtrack&nbsp;– Season 1 |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=legendsoftomorrow |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063656/https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=legendsoftomorrow |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> and the second on October 10, 2017.<ref>{{Cite web |title=DC's Legends Of Tomorrow: Season 2 (Original Television Soundtrack)) |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=dclegends2 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063656/https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=dclegends2 |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> In season 3, tracks from its episode of the "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]" event were included in the score soundtrack. ''DC{{'}}s Legends of Tomorrow: The Mixtape'' was released on August 20, 2021, featuring covers and original songs from the series to that point.<ref>{{Cite web |title=DC's Legends Of Tomorrow: The Mixtape (Songs from the Original Television Soundtrack) |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=DCLOT_Mixtape |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063655/https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=DCLOT_Mixtape |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> The soundtracks of the fourth and fifth seasons were released on September 5, 2021, the day of the sixth-season finale.<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 4, 2021 |title='DC's Legends of Tomorrow' Season 4 & 5 Soundtrack Albums Details |url=https://filmmusicreporter.com/2021/09/04/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-5-soundtrack-albums-details/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220107221457/https://filmmusicreporter.com/2021/09/04/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-4-5-soundtrack-albums-details/ |archive-date=January 7, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=Film Music Reporter}}</ref> Season six's soundtrack would be released on October 8, 2021.<ref>{{Cite web |title=DC's Legends Of Tomorrow: Season 6 (Original Television Soundtrack) |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=DCLOT_S6 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063655/https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=DCLOT_S6 |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> Season seven saw the release of three singles: "Future Favorite" from the episode "Speakeasy Does It" performed by [[Amy Pemberton]] and written by secondary composer James Chan, released on November 3, 2021,<ref>{{Cite web |title=Future Favorite (from DC's Legends of Tomorrow: Season 7) |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=LOT_FutureFavorite |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063432/https://www.watertower-music.com/tv/release.php?title=LOT_FutureFavorite |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> a polka-inspired cover of [[Dead or Alive (band)|Dead or Alive]]'s "[[You Spin Me Round (Like a Record)]]" performed by Jonathan Walton in the episode "The Fixed Point",<ref>{{Cite web |title=You Spin Me Round (Like a Record) [from "DC's Legends of Tomorrow: Season 7"] |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=DCLegendsYouSpin |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063431/https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=DCLegendsYouSpin |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref> and "By Your Side", performed by Shayan Sobhian as Behrad Tarazi in "Too Legit to Quit", both released on March 11, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |title=By My Side (from "DC's Legends of Tomorrow: Season 7") |url=https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=dclegendsbymyside |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220322063655/https://www.watertower-music.com/releases/release.php?title=dclegendsbymyside |archive-date=March 22, 2022 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |website=WaterTower Music}}</ref>

