The pilot was well reviewed for its potential. Russ Burlingame from ComicBook.com praised it saying, "The series delivers a sharp, enjoyable pilot that's arguably the most attention-grabbing and entertaining from any of the current crop of superhero shows."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=December 30, 2015 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Advance Review: The Best DC Pilot Yet |url=https://comicbook.com/news/legends-of-tomorrow-advance-review/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210514014558/https://comicbook.com/news/legends-of-tomorrow-advance-review/ |archive-date=May 14, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |publisher=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> Jesse Schedeen of [[IGN]] gave the first part of the pilot episode a 7.7/10, praising the show's "epic scope", "fun character dynamics", and Arthur Darvill's performance;<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=January 19, 2016 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow: "Pilot, Part 1" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/19/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-1-review |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160119214438/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/19/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-1-review |archive-date=January 19, 2016 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |publisher=IGN}}</ref> and gave the second part of the pilot an 8.4/10, saying it "improved in its sophomore episode thanks to great character dynamics and superhero action".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=January 29, 2016 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow: "Pilot, Part 2" Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/29/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-2-review |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160129033612/http://www.ign.com/articles/2016/01/29/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-pilot-part-2-review |archive-date=January 29, 2016 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |publisher=IGN}}</ref>

However, review aggregation website [[Rotten Tomatoes]] gave the complete first season only a 65% approval rating, with an average rating of 6.42/10 based on 36 reviews. The website's consensus reads: "Fancy effects, comic-book nostalgia, and an alluring cast help keep it afloat, but DC's ''Legends of Tomorrow'' suffers from an overloaded cast of characters that contribute to a distractingly crowded canvas."<ref name="S1RT" /> [[Metacritic]], which uses a weighted average, assigned a score of 58 out of 100 based on reviews from 22 critics, indicating "mixed or average reviews".<ref name="S1MC" />

Rotten Tomatoes gave the second season an 88% approval rating, with an average rating of 6.97/10 based on 10 reviews. The website's consensus reads: "Though the narrative remains too ambitious, DC's ''Legends of Tomorrow'' enjoys a freer creative arc with the removal of problem characters."<ref name="S2RT" />

The third season holds an approval rating of 88% on Rotten Tomatoes, with an average rating of 7.95/10 based on 8 reviews. The Website's consensus reads: "''DC's Legends of Tomorrow'' lightens up the tone in its third season while spotlighting adventurous plots and a distinct sense of humor."<ref name="S3RT" /> while IGN gave the season an approval rating of 8.1/10, stating: "When ''Legends of Tomorrow'' works, it's easily among the best superhero shows on television (if not shows in general). Unfortunately, while Season 3 reached some impressive highs, it also gave us some of the weakest installments of the series. Season 3 ultimately suffered from its inability to create a conflict worthy of this cast of misfit heroes, and that casts a shadow that will linger when the series returns for Season 4."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Schedeen |first=Jesse |date=April 19, 2018 |title=DC'S Legends of Tomorrow: Season 3 Review |url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2018/04/19/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-3-review |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180620181220/http://www.ign.com/articles/2018/04/19/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-season-3-review |archive-date=June 20, 2018 |access-date=June 20, 2018 |website=[[IGN]]}}</ref>

In April 2021, ''[[The A.V. Club]]'' praised the show's transformation to an "amazing metafictional comedy", calling it "one of the most impressive turnarounds in genre TV history."<ref>{{Cite web |date=April 29, 2021 |title=10 episodes that capture Legends Of Tomorrow's surprising transformation |url=https://www.avclub.com/10-episodes-that-take-dc-s-legends-of-tomorrow-from-bad-1846734454 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211209150235/https://www.avclub.com/10-episodes-that-take-dc-s-legends-of-tomorrow-from-bad-1846734454 |archive-date=December 9, 2021 |access-date=December 9, 2021 |website=The A.V. Club}}</ref>

