==Arrowverse==
{{main|Arrowverse|}}
In May 2015, Renée made a cameo in the final episode of ''The Flash''{{'}}s first season, "Fast Enough", and later made appearances in the show's second season in November 2015.<ref>{{Cite episode |title=Fast Enough |series=The Flash |series-link=The Flash (2014 TV series) |network=The CW |season=1 |number=23 |minutes=42}}</ref><ref>{{Cite episode |title=The Darkness and the Light |series=The Flash |series-link=The Flash (2014 TV series) |network=The CW |season=2 |number=5}}</ref><ref>{{Cite episode |title=Gorilla Warfare |series=The Flash |series-link=The Flash (2014 TV series) |network=The CW |season=2 |number=7}}</ref> In July 2015, Guggenheim revealed that the resurrection of Sara Lance would be launched in the first few episodes of ''Arrow''{{'}}s fourth season, with the events of the eighth episodes of ''Arrow'' and ''The Flash''—which were a crossover event—being used to set up the other characters of ''Legends of Tomorrow''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=July 21, 2015 |title=Spoiler Chat: Scoop on American Horror Story, Pretty Little Liars, Arrow, The Mindy Project and More! |url=http://www.eonline.com/news/678116/spoiler-chat-scoop-on-american-horror-story-pretty-little-liars-arrow-the-mindy-project-and-more |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150723073754/http://www.eonline.com/news/678116/spoiler-chat-scoop-on-american-horror-story-pretty-little-liars-arrow-the-mindy-project-and-more |archive-date=July 23, 2015 |access-date=July 22, 2015 |publisher=E! Online}}</ref> Franz Drameh was introduced as the new other half of Firestorm in the fourth episode of the second season of ''The Flash''. Crump, Hentschel and James debut in the crossover episodes for the second season of ''The Flash'' and the fourth season of ''Arrow''.<ref name="Hentschel" /><ref name="Crump" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=September 24, 2015 |title=EXCLUSIVE: Legends of Tomorrow Casts Peter Francis James As Key Part of Hawkman/Hawkgirl Story |url=https://comicbook.com/news/exclusive-legends-of-tomorrow-casts-peter-francis-james-as-key-p/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161205032204/http://comicbook.com/2015/09/24/exclusive-legends-of-tomorrow-casts-peter-francis-james-as-key-p/ |archive-date=December 5, 2016 |access-date=March 22, 2022 |publisher=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> In November 2016, the cast of ''Legends of Tomorrow'' appeared on ''The Flash'' and ''Arrow'' as part of the "[[Invasion! (Arrowverse)|Invasion!]]" crossover event, which also featured appearances by [[Melissa Benoist]], reprising her role as [[Kara Danvers (Arrowverse)|Kara Danvers / Supergirl]] from ''[[Supergirl (TV series)|Supergirl]]''.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Abrams |first=Natalie |date=2016-05-19 |title=The CW announces four-way crossover with 'Arrow,' 'The Flash,' 'Legends of Tomorrow,' 'Supergirl' |url=https://ew.com/article/2016/05/19/cw-crossover-arrow-flash-legends-tomorrow-supergirl/ |access-date=2022-11-08 |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |language=en |archive-date=November 8, 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221108031327/https://ew.com/article/2016/05/19/cw-crossover-arrow-flash-legends-tomorrow-supergirl/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Further crossovers occurred with "[[Crisis on Earth-X]]" in 2017,<ref>{{cite magazine |date=September 22, 2017 |title=Arrow, The Flash, Supergirl, Legends to unite for 'Crisis on Earth-X' crossover |url=https://ew.com/tv/2017/09/22/arrow-the-flash-supergirl-legends-unite-for-crisis-on-earth-x-crossover/ |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170923002507/http://ew.com/tv/2017/09/22/arrow-the-flash-supergirl-legends-unite-for-crisis-on-earth-x-crossover/ |archive-date=September 23, 2017 |access-date=February 22, 2018}}</ref> and "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" in-between 2019 and 2020.<ref name="CrisisOnInfiniteEarthsCrossover">{{cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=December 11, 2018 |title=Arrowverse Crossover Title for Fall 2019 (!) Is Revealed — And It Is a Doozy |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/arrowverse-crossover-title-2019-crisis-on-infinite-earths-1010874/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181212024818/https://tvline.com/2018/12/11/arrowverse-crossover-title-2019-crisis-on-infinite-earths/ |archive-date=December 12, 2018 |access-date=December 11, 2018 |work=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>
