==Christmas special==
The series' breakout toy character Beebo, voiced by [[Benjamin Diskin]], starred in his own Christmas special, titled ''Beebo Saves Christmas'', which aired on December 21, 2021. Narrated by Victor Garber, the special sees Diskin reprising his role, alongside [[Ernie Hudson]] as [[Santa Claus]], [[Chris Kattan]] as a [[Christmas elf]] named Sprinkles, [[Kimiko Glenn]] as Tweebo, [[Yvette Nicole Brown]] as Turbo, and [[Keith Ferguson (voice actor)|Keith Ferguson]] as Fleabo.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=May 25, 2021 |title='Legends of Tomorrow' breakout Beebo is getting an animated Christmas special on the CW |url=https://ew.com/tv/legends-of-tomorrow-beebo-saves-christmas-special/ |url-status=live |magazine=Entertainment Weekly |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211016003742/https://ew.com/tv/legends-of-tomorrow-beebo-saves-christmas-special/ |archive-date=October 16, 2021 |access-date=October 15, 2021}}</ref>

== Cancellation ==
Ahead of the season seven finale, Shimizu said it was not intended to be the [[series finale]] even though an eighth season had not yet been ordered.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gelman |first=Vlada |date=March 1, 2022 |title=Legends Boss Says 'Propulsive' Finale Is Not Intended as Series Ender, Teases Donald Faison's Mystery Character |url=https://www.tvline.com/previews/legends-of-tomorrow-spoilers-season-7-finale-renewed-cancelled-1234801966/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220525212008/https://tvline.com/2022/03/01/legends-of-tomorrow-spoilers-season-7-finale-renewed-cancelled/ |archive-date=May 25, 2022 |access-date=June 10, 2022 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref> Despite this, The CW canceled the series on April 29, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Shafer |first=Ellise |date=April 29, 2022 |title='DC's Legends of Tomorrow' Canceled at the CW |url=https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-canceled-the-cw-1235254994/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220430015006/https://variety.com/2022/tv/news/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-canceled-the-cw-1235254994/ |archive-date=April 30, 2022 |access-date=April 30, 2022 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Shortly thereafter, fans began campaigning to save the series by renewing it for an eighth and final season to wrap up the series' loose ends.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Burlingame |first=Russ |date=May 13, 2022 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Fans Bought a Billboard in New York City to Save the Show |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/legends-of-tomorrow-fans-bought-a-billboard-in-new-york-city-to-save-the-show/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230212124951/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/legends-of-tomorrow-fans-bought-a-billboard-in-new-york-city-to-save-the-show/ |archive-date=February 12, 2023 |access-date=June 22, 2023 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> Shimizu held herself responsible for the series ending without proper resolution, explaining that her contract ended with the season but she did not want to reveal anything until the series was renewed for an eighth season; she conceded that she "[[wikt:play chicken|played chicken]] with the pickup, and lost", but was hopeful the loose ends could be resolved through other means such as a comic book tie-in, television film, or radio play.<ref name="unresolved">{{Cite web |last=Drum |first=Nicole |date=April 30, 2022 |title=DC's Legends of Tomorrow Co-Showrunner Addresses Series' Cliffhanger Ending |url=https://comicbook.com/dc/news/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-co-showrunner-keto-shimizu-addresses-series-cliffhanger-ending/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220603033100/https://comicbook.com/dc/news/dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-co-showrunner-keto-shimizu-addresses-series-cliffhanger-ending/ |archive-date=June 3, 2022 |access-date=June 10, 2022 |website=[[ComicBook.com]]}}</ref> The introduction of [[Booster Gold]], played by [[Donald Faison]] in the season seven finale, was meant to deter The CW from canceling the series, and Faison would have been a main cast member had an eighth season been ordered.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermanns |first=Grant |date=May 9, 2022 |title=Booster Gold Was Intended To Save Legends of Tomorrow, Says Co-Showrunner |url=https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-show-cancelled-booster-gold-story-details/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220613012116/https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-show-cancelled-booster-gold-story-details/ |archive-date=June 13, 2022 |access-date=June 27, 2022 |website=[[Screen Rant]]}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Behbakht |first=Andy |date=March 3, 2022 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Season 8 Would Make New DC Hero A Main Character |url=https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-season-8-booster-gold-donald-faison/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220610212807/https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-season-8-booster-gold-donald-faison/ |archive-date=June 10, 2022 |access-date=June 27, 2022 |website=[[Screen Rant]]}}</ref> The tie-in comic ''Earth-Prime: Legends of Tomorrow #3'' has a storyline set after the series finale, which ''[[Screen Rant]]'' writer Matt Morrison believed should give fans of the series some form of closure.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Morrison |first=Matt |date=May 4, 2022 |title=Legends of Tomorrow Reveals Heroes' Final Fate in Arrowverse Continuity |url=https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-arrowverse-future-earth-1-canary-wally/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220627061018/https://screenrant.com/legends-tomorrow-arrowverse-future-earth-1-canary-wally/ |archive-date=June 27, 2022 |access-date=August 6, 2026 |work=[[Screen Rant]]}}</ref>

Lesley Goldberg of ''[[The Hollywood Reporter]]'' noted that although CW chairman [[Mark Pedowitz]] wanted the series to continue, [[Warner Bros. Television Studios|Warner Bros. Television]] did not want to continue paying the leases on the studio space, which were set to expire on May 1, leading to the series' cancellation. Having the series continue on [[HBO Max]] or [[Paramount+]] was considered impossible by Goldberg due to the series being part of a deal Warner Bros. signed with [[Netflix]] in 2011.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Goldberg |first=Lesley |date=May 13, 2022 |title=Mad About The CW Cancellations? Blame Streaming, But Also Its Unusual Corporate Structure |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/the-cw-cancellations-blame-streaming-but-also-its-unusual-corporate-structure-1235146038/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220610022440/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/the-cw-cancellations-blame-streaming-but-also-its-unusual-corporate-structure-1235146038/ |archive-date=June 10, 2022 |access-date=June 10, 2022 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> With ''The Flash'' being the last remaining Arrowverse series at the time, its showrunner Eric Wallace expressed interest in the series' [[The Flash season 9|ninth season]] trying to resolve the loose ends left behind by ''Legends of Tomorrow'', but was uncertain of the viability because the number of episodes for the season had not yet been decided, and he believed incorporating the Legends was difficult to achieve when he had to conclude his own story.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=May 30, 2022 |title=The Flash EP Would Love to Rescue the Imprisoned, Cancelled Legends, But.... |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/the-flash-season-9-crossover-rescue-cancelled-legends-of-tomorrow-time-jail-1234832065/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220718101619/https://tvline.com/2022/05/30/the-flash-season-9-crossover-rescue-cancelled-legends-of-tomorrow-time-jail/ |archive-date=July 18, 2022 |access-date=July 18, 2022 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref> Upon his hiring as the co-chairman and co-CEO of [[DC Studios]] in November 2022, [[James Gunn]] acknowledged campaigns calling to save the series, but also stated that his focus at the time would not be on [[Revival (television)|revivals]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovich |first=Matt Webb |date=November 6, 2022 |title=New DC Studios Boss James Gunn Addresses Calls to 'Save' Legends and Others, Teases Scope of 'New DCU' |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/will-james-gunn-save-legends-of-tomorrow-batwoman-1234895265/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221108225356/https://tvline.com/2022/11/06/will-james-gunn-save-legends-of-tomorrow-batwoman/ |archive-date=November 8, 2022 |access-date=November 7, 2022 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref> The ninth season of ''The Flash'' ultimately did not feature the Legends or close any loose ends as originally intended due to being constrained by the 13-episode limit.<ref>{{Cite web |date=February 6, 2023 |title=Showrunner Eric Wallace on the Beginning of the End of the 'The Flash' |url=https://thenerdsofcolor.org/2023/02/06/showrunner-eric-wallace-on-the-beginning-of-the-end-of-the-the-flash/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230214110817/https://thenerdsofcolor.org/2023/02/06/showrunner-eric-wallace-on-the-beginning-of-the-end-of-the-the-flash/ |archive-date=February 14, 2023 |access-date=February 14, 2023 |website=The Nerds of Color}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Opie |first=David |date=May 24, 2023 |title=Why The Flash and the entire Arrowverse has been cancelled |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a43947095/the-flash-cancelled-season-10-arrowverse/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231007163635/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/ustv/a43947095/the-flash-cancelled-season-10-arrowverse/ |archive-date=October 7, 2023 |access-date=April 26, 2024 |website=[[Digital Spy]] |language=en}}</ref> Guggenheim stated in May 2026 that the CW, under Pedowitz, wanted to conclude the storyline of ''Legends of Tomorrow'' with a film, but the proposal was rejected by Warner Bros.<ref>{{Cite web |last=DeArmitt |first=Grant |date=May 26, 2026 |title=The CW wanted a Legends of Tomorrow movie to wrap up the show's story - Warner Bros. said no |url=https://www.thepopverse.com/tv-the-legends-of-tomorrow-cw-movies-season-7-finale-marc-guggenheim-warner-bros |access-date=June 2, 2026 |website=[[PopVerse]] |archive-date=May 27, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260527164913/https://www.thepopverse.com/tv-the-legends-of-tomorrow-cw-movies-season-7-finale-marc-guggenheim-warner-bros |url-status=live }}</ref>

